{
  "title": "Piano Practice",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Read",
      "lines": [
        "Notes scroll right to",
        "left on a treble staff.",
        "Play the pad as the note",
        "crosses the line.",
        "",
        "On time: the notehead",
        "turns into a circle.",
        "Missed: it turns into",
        "an X.",
        "",
        "A circle also marks where",
        "you actually played. In",
        "time, it lands on the",
        "note as one mark. Late,",
        "you see two and the gap",
        "is your error.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops and names",
        "it on screen. At stage 1",
        "the pad you need pulses",
        "white.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops on it. The X",
        "stays by the line however",
        "far ahead you are reading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lessons",
      "lines": [
        "The list is in folders.",
        "CLICK opens one, BACK",
        "goes up one, and BACK at",
        "the top leaves.",
        "",
        "Learning Program",
        "  what to play next.",
        "Basics",
        "  scales in all 22 of",
        "  Move's scales, every",
        "  chord on all twelve",
        "  roots, progressions in",
        "  your key, and random",
        "  notes and chords.",
        "Quiz",
        "  Hear: name a sound.",
        "  Play: find it on pads.",
        "  Name: name a lit pad.",
        "Classics",
        "  folk tunes and the",
        "  classics, easy first.",
        "Electronic",
        "  the chords of famous",
        "  tracks, never the tune.",
        "Techno",
        "  the classic progressions",
        "  and stabs, simple first.",
        "Styles",
        "  pop, soul, funk, film.",
        "Progress",
        "  at the bottom.",
        "",
        "Every row shows how far",
        "you have got: a percent,",
        "a half circle for stage",
        "1, a tick for stage 2.",
        "",
        "Every song fits one page",
        "of pads, both hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Info",
      "lines": [
        "MENU explains what is in",
        "front of you: a row of",
        "the list, the armed",
        "exercise, a quiz, a",
        "result. It says what the",
        "practice asks and what",
        "its words mean.",
        "",
        "JOG scrolls. BACK or",
        "MENU closes it, back to",
        "where you were.",
        "",
        "A quiz's clock stops",
        "while you read, and a",
        "running piece pauses.",
        "",
        "The first time you open",
        "a kind of practice, its",
        "Info shows by itself.",
        "Auto info in settings",
        "turns that off.",
        "",
        "Quiz sounds: a chime",
        "when right, an uh-oh",
        "when wrong."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Levels",
      "lines": [
        "A song has up to four",
        "levels. Pick the song,",
        "then pick the level.",
        "",
        "L1 RH melody",
        "  the right hand alone,",
        "  one note at a time.",
        "L1 LH bass",
        "  the left hand alone,",
        "  the bass line.",
        "L2 RH chords",
        "  the melody with its",
        "  chords under it.",
        "L3 Both hands",
        "  the two together.",
        "",
        "All four sit in the same",
        "register. The pads you",
        "learn at L1 are the pads",
        "you play at L3.",
        "",
        "Back from a song goes to",
        "its levels, not all the",
        "way out to the songs.",
        "",
        "A chord lesson's L1 RH is",
        "its top voice, L1 LH the",
        "roots. Inversions are one",
        "hand, so they have two."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Stages",
      "lines": [
        "Every exercise has two",
        "stages.",
        "",
        "Stage 1",
        "  the pad you need next",
        "  lights up as the note",
        "  comes. Learn the shape.",
        "Stage 2",
        "  nothing lights up. Read",
        "  it from the staff.",
        "",
        "90% or better passes a",
        "stage, at any tempo.",
        "Stage 1 earns a half",
        "circle, stage 2 a tick.",
        "",
        "An exercise opens on the",
        "first stage you have not",
        "passed. Turn the JOG on",
        "the ready screen to pick",
        "the other one - you can",
        "go straight to stage 2.",
        "",
        "Score: notes hit over",
        "notes plus wrong presses.",
        "A row shows your latest",
        "run, but once a stage is",
        "passed it never drops.",
        "",
        "Only a run from the top",
        "counts. Start from a",
        "scrubbed bar to practise",
        "a passage off the record.",
        "",
        "In a quiz, stage 1 is a",
        "round with hints, stage",
        "2 a round without."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Program",
      "lines": [
        "Learning Program is a",
        "path through everything.",
        "Nothing is locked: play",
        "anything, in any order.",
        "It still counts.",
        "",
        "Four tracks run side by",
        "side:",
        "Reading  scales, lines,",
        "         first tunes",
        "Chords   triads to",
        "         altered, and",
        "         progressions",
        "Songs    every piece,",
        "         rung by rung",
        "Ear      the quiz drills",
        "",
        "Continue opens the next",
        "step of the track you",
        "left longest. The next",
        "step is the first one",
        "not done and not skipped.",
        "",
        "Skip passes the next",
        "step by. If stage 1 is",
        "passed it moves on",
        "instead: stage 1 is",
        "enough for now.",
        "",
        "Repetition brings back",
        "finished exercises: any",
        "that slipped under 90%,",
        "then ones due again -",
        "after 1, 3, 7, 14, then",
        "30 days. A repeat never",
        "lowers a finished score."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quiz",
      "lines": [
        "The Quiz folder has",
        "three: Hear, Play, Name.",
        "Play > notes / chords",
        "One note or chord sits",
        "still on the staff, named",
        "below it, until you play",
        "it. No clock, no timing.",
        "",
        "Hear > Play it back",
        "The same, but you hear it",
        "instead of seeing it. The",
        "staff shows a ? until you",
        "play it right, then it",
        "reveals what it was.",
        "",
        "Both drill finding a",
        "pitch on the grid, which",
        "is its own skill: the",
        "pads go up in fifths, so",
        "the same note sits in",
        "several places.",
        "",
        "A chord must be held all",
        "at once. Part of it down",
        "is not yet a mistake.",
        "",
        "Name > notes / chords",
        "A pad lights and you name",
        "it, choosing with the",
        "jog. Click to answer.",
        "The other two are",
        "near misses - a semitone",
        "away, or the same chord",
        "root with another quality",
        "- so a rough sense of",
        "high or low will not do.",
        "",
        "This is the only mode",
        "that goes pad to name,",
        "and the only one you can",
        "do without playing.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear it",
        "REC    help, twice",
        "BACK   back to the list",
        "",
        "Half tones adds the black",
        "notes to the note pools.",
        "On by default: they are",
        "the hard ones to find.",
        "",
        "Chords: triads asks the",
        "diatonic triads of the",
        "key. types asks a chosen",
        "quality - dim, aug, sus,",
        "6, 7, maj7, m7, m7b5,",
        "dim7, add9. advanced adds",
        "ninths and altered",
        "dominants: 9, maj9, m9,",
        "6/9, 7b5, 7#5, 7b9, 7#9,",
        "7sus4, 9sus4, mMaj7.",
        "",
        "Both the chord symbol and",
        "its notes are shown, so",
        "you learn what the shape",
        "under your hands is",
        "called. A scale that",
        "stacks something that is",
        "not a chord shows the",
        "notes with no symbol.",
        "",
        "The answer is never lit",
        "on the pads. Stage 1",
        "lights pads for playing,",
        "never in a quiz.",
        "",
        "REC gives help, two",
        "presses deep. Hearing:",
        "names it, then lights the",
        "pads. Reading: sounds it,",
        "then lights the pads.",
        "Picking: strikes out one",
        "wrong option, then the",
        "other.",
        "",
        "Hinted answers still count",
        "and keep the streak, but",
        "the round records how many",
        "you took."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Answers",
      "lines": [
        "A Hear drill that asks",
        "what you heard turns",
        "the bottom pads into",
        "answer buttons, each its",
        "own colour. The screen",
        "says which is which.",
        "",
        "2-4 answers: every other",
        "pad, so a near miss hits",
        "a dark pad.",
        "5-8: the whole bottom",
        "row. 9-12: two rows. The",
        "screen then draws a map",
        "of the pads.",
        "",
        "Press a pad to answer.",
        "It plays no note. The",
        "other pads still play.",
        "",
        "JOG and CLICK work too.",
        "The jog's answer pulses",
        "on its pad.",
        "",
        "Name keeps the jog: its",
        "lit pads are the question",
        "and stay pressable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hearing",
      "lines": [
        "Quiz > Hear, and the",
        "Hearing track of the",
        "Learning Program. You hear",
        "something and name it -",
        "nothing to read, nothing",
        "lit. Easiest first:",
        "",
        "1 Higher or lower",
        "2 Play it back",
        "3 Step or leap",
        "4 Melody shape",
        "5 Major or minor 3rd",
        "6 Major/minor chord",
        "7 Perfect intervals",
        "8 2nds and 3rds",
        "9 Intervals up",
        "10 Intervals down",
        "11 Intervals together",
        "12 Four triads",
        "13 Major or minor key",
        "14 Home or away",
        "15 Scale degrees",
        "16 Seventh chords",
        "17 Chords in a key",
        "18 Play the chord",
        "",
        "Each has levels, easy to",
        "hard: melodic before",
        "together, up before down,",
        "broken chords before",
        "block ones.",
        "",
        "Press its answer pad.",
        "The answers keep their",
        "order, so where one sits",
        "becomes habit. A long list",
        "scrolls; the marks at the",
        "right say there is more.",
        "",
        "The root changes every",
        "time: listen to the",
        "distance, not the note.",
        "",
        "Right: the pads flash and",
        "the notes are named.",
        "Wrong: counted once, and",
        "the question stays.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear it again",
        "REC    help, twice",
        "BACK   back to the list",
        "",
        "REC 1 plays it slower,",
        "chords broken up first.",
        "REC 2 strikes out a wrong",
        "answer.",
        "",
        "2 and 18 are the Hear",
        "drills: play back what",
        "you heard on the pads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rounds",
      "lines": [
        "A quiz is a round of 20",
        "prompts (10/20/30 in",
        "settings, or endless).",
        "",
        "The clock starts on your",
        "first press, not when the",
        "screen appears. A prompt",
        "waits until you get it",
        "right, so a wrong answer",
        "costs you time rather",
        "than a penalty - the same",
        "way a typing test treats",
        "a typo.",
        "",
        "The result is correct",
        "answers per minute, your",
        "error rate, and a chart",
        "of recent rounds.",
        "",
        "endless records nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Results",
      "lines": [
        "A finished run shows the",
        "percent you got right",
        "and a chart of every",
        "recent attempt: hollow",
        "points are stage 1,",
        "solid ones stage 2. The",
        "dotted line is 90%.",
        "",
        "REC  play it again",
        "BACK back to the start,",
        "     then BACK to the list",
        "CLICK  next: stage 2 if",
        "     you just passed stage",
        "     1, else the next step",
        "SHIFT+CLICK  move on, or",
        "     skip it",
        "",
        "Progress, at the bottom",
        "of the list: Overall and",
        "each track plot stages",
        "passed over time. Then",
        "everything you played,",
        "newest first. CLICK a",
        "row for its chart, JOG",
        "for the next.",
        "",
        "A quiz drill plots its",
        "rate as a line and its",
        "errors as bars. A full",
        "bar is 50% wrong."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Play",
      "lines": [
        "PLAY   listen. The",
        "  exercise plays itself",
        "  and the pads light up",
        "  as it goes, so you can",
        "  watch it before you",
        "  try it. Nothing scored.",
        "REC    practice. You",
        "  play it, it scores you.",
        "",
        "Both pulse when ready.",
        "The one that is running",
        "goes solid.",
        "",
        "KNOB 1 scrubs through",
        "the piece before you",
        "start, and the pads light",
        "the note you landed on.",
        "PLAY or REC then",
        "begins from where you",
        "left it, with no count-in",
        "and no misses for the",
        "bars you skipped over.",
        "BACK returns to the top.",
        "",
        "JOG    pick, in the list",
        "CLICK  open the folder",
        "MENU   info",
        "BACK   up one level",
        "SHIFT + BACK   close",
        "",
        "shift + jog: settings",
        "",
        "Four beats count you in,",
        "counted on screen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sound",
      "lines": [
        "The module has its own",
        "piano. It is the default",
        "and needs no setup: no",
        "track, no instrument, no",
        "MIDI channel to match.",
        "It mixes in alongside",
        "whatever else Move is",
        "playing.",
        "",
        "MIDI out can send",
        "elsewhere instead:",
        "track  a Move track,",
        "  on the MIDI ch below",
        "  (all = every channel)",
        "USB    the USB-A port",
        "trk+USB  both of those",
        "",
        "Closing silences the",
        "piano and every channel",
        "on both MIDI routes,",
        "then waits for it to",
        "drain before letting go.",
        "SHIFT + BACK closes",
        "from anywhere."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT + CLICK opens",
        "settings. CLICK a row to",
        "edit it, turn to change,",
        "CLICK again when done.",
        "",
        "Wait stops the scroll at",
        "a note until you play it.",
        "On by default.",
        "",
        "The scroll always halts",
        "ON the note it wants,",
        "so you can see what it",
        "is asking for. A missed",
        "chord is named under",
        "the staff, not over it.",
        "",
        "PLAY again pauses where",
        "you are. Knob 1 scrubs",
        "whenever the music is",
        "not running - paused, or",
        "before you begin -",
        "smoothly, about 1.5",
        "turns per bar. PLAY",
        "carries on from there,",
        "so you can take a bar",
        "twice. BACK restarts;",
        "twice leaves. Knob 8",
        "is tempo.",
        "",
        "Grace is how late you",
        "may play it and still",
        "count, in beats - so it",
        "scales with tempo. One",
        "beat by default: time",
        "to find the key. 2 or 4",
        "while a piece is new,",
        "1/4 when the rhythm is",
        "the point. Later than",
        "that still releases the",
        "scroll, but scores a",
        "miss.",
        "",
        "Any octave accepts the",
        "right note in the wrong",
        "register.",
        "",
        "Exercises live in the",
        "exercises folder. Add a",
        "JSON file and list it",
        "in index.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Terms",
      "lines": [
        "Semitone",
        "  The smallest step: the",
        "  next pad to the right.",
        "",
        "Tone",
        "  Two semitones. W",
        "  (whole) in a step",
        "  pattern; a semitone is",
        "  H (half).",
        "",
        "Octave",
        "  The same note 12",
        "  semitones up. On the",
        "  pads: two rows up, two",
        "  right.",
        "",
        "Sharp, flat",
        "  # raises a note a",
        "  semitone, b lowers it.",
        "  C# and Db are one pad.",
        "",
        "Scale",
        "  Notes climbing from a",
        "  root by a fixed pattern",
        "  of tones and semitones.",
        "",
        "Key",
        "  The scale a piece is",
        "  built from, named by",
        "  its root: G major, A",
        "  minor.",
        "",
        "Root",
        "  The note a scale or",
        "  chord is named after",
        "  and built on.",
        "",
        "Tonic",
        "  The root of the key:",
        "  home. A tune ending",
        "  there sounds finished.",
        "",
        "Degree",
        "  A note's place in the",
        "  scale, counted from the",
        "  root: 1 to 7.",
        "",
        "Interval",
        "  The distance between",
        "  two notes, named by the",
        "  letters it spans: C-E",
        "  spans C D E, a 3rd.",
        "",
        "Major, minor",
        "  Interval sizes. A major",
        "  3rd is 4 semitones, a",
        "  minor 3rd 3. Major",
        "  sounds brighter.",
        "",
        "Perfect",
        "  4ths, 5ths and octaves:",
        "  the most stable",
        "  intervals, neither",
        "  major nor minor.",
        "",
        "Tritone",
        "  6 semitones, half an",
        "  octave. Tense,",
        "  unresolved.",
        "",
        "Step",
        "  Two neighbouring notes",
        "  of the scale, a 2nd",
        "  apart: C-D.",
        "",
        "Leap",
        "  Two scale notes further",
        "  apart than a step, a",
        "  3rd or more: C-E.",
        "",
        "Contour",
        "  The shape of a melody:",
        "  which way each note",
        "  moves.",
        "",
        "Chord",
        "  Three or more notes",
        "  sounding together.",
        "",
        "Triad",
        "  Three notes stacked in",
        "  3rds: root, 3rd, 5th.",
        "  C-E-G is C major.",
        "",
        "Quality",
        "  What kind a chord is:",
        "  major, minor,",
        "  diminished, seventh...",
        "",
        "Formula",
        "  A chord's notes as",
        "  degrees of the root's",
        "  major scale: minor is 1",
        "  b3 5.",
        "",
        "Inversion",
        "  A chord with another of",
        "  its notes at the",
        "  bottom. C/E is C major",
        "  over E.",
        "",
        "Seventh chord",
        "  A triad with a 7th on",
        "  top: four notes.",
        "",
        "Voicing",
        "  Which octave each note",
        "  of a chord sits in, and",
        "  in which hand.",
        "",
        "Broken, block",
        "  Broken: a chord's notes",
        "  one after another.",
        "  Block: all at once.",
        "",
        "Progression",
        "  A sequence of chords,",
        "  named by Roman numerals",
        "  for the degree each",
        "  starts on: I, IV, V.",
        "",
        "Roman numerals",
        "  I is the chord on",
        "  degree 1. Upper case is",
        "  major, lower case",
        "  minor: vi is minor.",
        "",
        "Slash chord",
        "  A chord over a bass",
        "  note that is not its",
        "  root: D/F# is D major",
        "  over F#.",
        "",
        "RH, LH",
        "  Right hand plays the",
        "  melody and chords, left",
        "  hand the bass.",
        "",
        "Level",
        "  How much of a song you",
        "  play: L1 one hand's",
        "  line, L2 the chords, L3",
        "  both hands.",
        "",
        "Stage",
        "  Stage 1 lights each pad",
        "  as its note comes.",
        "  Stage 2 lights nothing:",
        "  you read.",
        "",
        "Score",
        "  Notes hit, over the",
        "  notes in the piece plus",
        "  wrong presses. 90%",
        "  passes a stage.",
        "",
        "Hint",
        "  REC helps, two presses",
        "  deep. A hinted answer",
        "  still counts, and is",
        "  noted."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
